course: dictionary
lesson: 13616
title: Indicate: show, sign or signal
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Indicate» is a verb, so it can change: indicate, indicates, indicated, indicating. Its first meaning is to show or point to something. «The arrow on the map indicates the way to the lake.» The arrow points, so it shows the way.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning. «Dark clouds indicate that rain is coming.» Here indicate means to be a sign that something is true or likely. The clouds do not point at anything. They are a clue that rain will probably come.
explain: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, indicate can mean to show which way you will turn in a car, using the lights. «Always indicate before you turn.» Read the words around it: the car is turning, so the meaning is about lights, not pointing.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. Does «point to» fit? Does «is a sign that» fit? Does «show which way with the lights» fit? The one that makes sense is the right meaning.
fact: Indicate is a verb: indicate, indicates, indicated, indicating.
fact: «Indicate» means to show or point to something.
fact: «Indicate» can also mean to be a sign that something is true or likely: «The graph indicates a rise in temperature.»
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, «indicate» means to show which way you will turn in a car, using the lights.
fact: In formal writing, «indicate» can mean to state something briefly: «The letter indicated that the trip was cancelled.»
exercise: «The arrow on the map indicates the way to the lake.» What does indicates mean here? | Measures the distance | Hides | Breaks | *Points to or shows
exercise: «Dark clouds indicate that rain is coming.» What does indicate mean here? | Washes the car | *Is a sign that rain is likely | Makes the rain stop | Is a kind of cloud
exercise: In a car, what does «indicate left» mean? | Drive on the left side only | Stop the car at once | Sound the horn twice | *Switch on the left turn lights to show you will turn left
test: In «As indicated, the answer is 12», what does indicated mean? | Painted | Counted twice | Lost | *Shown or pointed out
test: In «Always indicate before you turn», what does indicate mean? | Shout your turn to other cars | *Show which way you will turn, using your lights | Slow down to a stop | Turn the engine off
exam: «The formal letter indicated that the trip was cancelled.» What does indicated mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Forgot about | Drew a picture of | *Stated briefly
